      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Ilioinguinal nerve entrapment is a documented complication of inguinal herniorrhaphy, inguinal lymph node dissection, and appendectomy. This article reports two clinical histories to illustrate the diagnosis and management, and outlines prevention of ilioinguinal nerve entrapment as a complication of needle suspension procedures for stress urinary incontinence."},
